        "original_id": "fb4e5c20-d70e-563f-8aac-3ca1bb3d5656",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Spirit of '45\n- People: Ken Loach, Clement Attlee\n- Roles: Prime Minister of the United Kingdom, Leader of the Labour Party\n- Topics: postwar Britain, Labour government\n\nFacts:\n- Clement Attlee was born on 3 January 1883 and died on 8 October 1967.\n- Clement Attlee was a British Labour politician who served as Leader of the Labour Party from 1935 to 1955.\n- Clement Attlee served as Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from 1945 to 1951.\n- Clement Attlee led the Labour government that came to power in Britain in 1945.\n- The Spirit of '45 is a 2013 documentary film directed by British director Ken Loach.\n- The Spirit of '45 focuses on and celebrates the radical changes in postwar Britain under the Labour government of Clement Attlee.",
